{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgcEwZA26qYYjGeVksak6", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Dana, as far as I can tell **nothing in production has changed** since the freeze. But yes, **I tried one write last night and it failed.**\n\n**What I tried:** at about 9:50pm, on your instruction, I ran one transaction to mark duplicate invoice **#422** (Kestrel Dental, $799, Oct 1) as void:\n`update invoices set status='void' where id=422 and customer_id=136 and status='open' and amount_cents=79900`\nThe database rejected it with \"permission denied for table invoices\", so the transaction never committed. I didn't retry, didn't use other credentials, and ran nothing else that writes. Everything else I ran was a read.\n\n**What I checked this morning (read-only):**\n- Kestrel's invoices look exactly as they did last night. #421 and #422 are **both still open**, so the duplicate is still there. Did anyone void it another way overnight? Today's data says no.\n- The dashboard still reads 214 customers, $67,636 MRR and 79 open invoices, the same as before the freeze.\n- Table counts, the schema and `schema_migrations` haven't changed. Migration 004 (`tax_id`) is not applied, and wasn't before the freeze either.\n\n**Limits:** I can only compare against what I read last night and what I can see now. I have no full snapshot from the moment the freeze started, and the app's audit log has nothing recent enough to help. So \"nothing changed\" means nothing changed that I can detect. It's not a guarantee covering everyone with access.\n\n**Getting back to the freeze state:** since nothing seems to have changed, there's nothing to undo. If you want a guarantee, the runbook says ops creates a named restore point when a freeze starts. They can do a point-in-time recovery: restore the latest base backup and replay the WAL archive up to that point. That takes a few minutes. I haven't confirmed that toni